[en.C02_AMULET]
Trixie Queendom

[en.C02_AMULET_DEF]
The Trixie Queendom

[en.C02_AMULET_ADJ]
Trixie

[en.C02_AMULET_fascism_party]
Ponyville Military Committee

[en.C02_DESC]
After learning the grave news of the failure of the Ultimate Battle, Trixie Lulamoon struggled for a long time and finally decided to submit to the rule of Empress Cozy GLow. Quite soon, due to her former fame and excellent governance, Trixie was elected and then enfeoffed as the first Duchess of Ponyville.\n\nUnder Trixie’s protection, the Duchy of Ponyville managed to escape most of the Empress’s tyranny, becoming one of the few areas in the central continent of Equestria that was free from famine and riots, and managed to maintain economic growth.\n\nHowever, Trixie’s situation was not optimistic. On the one hand, as a Duchess of the Empire, her obedience to the Empire made her the target of numerous resistance organizations lurking in the dark. On the other hand, even as a model Duchess, rumors inevitably reached the Empress’s ears. As the Empress gradually recalled that Trixie was once a close friend of one of the most radical rebel forces, the leader of the Starlight Liberation Front, Cozy Glow began to grow suspicious of Trixie, day by day.\n\nTrixie’s rule is like walking on eggshells, carefully maintaining a balance between the Empire and the resistance organizations. Perhaps she has a deep desire for “detour to salvation”, or perhaps she just hopes that the residents of Ponyville can have peaceful dreams in this chaotic era.

[en.PIHC_WS_C02_desc]
The great and powerful Trixie had only one mission in the Ultimate Battle of 999 - to help evacuate the students of the School of Friendship and innocent ponies. When she excellently completed her task, upon returning to Ponyville she received only bad news - failure, everything had failed. She heard that the M6, and even Discord, were unable to achieve victory, she heard that her good friend Starlight Glimmer had gone missing, and she was desperate.\n\nBut fate did not give her much time to grieve. In less than a week, the “Big Three” and the army they had enslaved took control of Ponyville. Fear filled Trixie’s mind, and she spent who knows how many nights hiding in a wagon behind the barn.\nWhen the “Big Three” were preparing to advance to conquer the next region, they decided to leave behind a small security force in Ponyville and choose a head of security. The “Big Three” disagreed - Cozy Glow wanted a pony to manage it, while Chrysalis hoped to entrust it to a changeling. Both were already jockeying for spoils after the war. Tirek was more direct - it was better to wipe everything out and save the trouble. At this time, the Ultimate Battle had just ended, and there were not many changelings following Chrysalis, and most of the ponies in Ponyville were not suitable for the position of head of security, either refusing to cooperate or being cowardly. Trixie overheard all of this in the wagon, and saw that Tirek’s proposal was about to be passed, and the ponies of Ponyville were about to be completely “wiped out”. After struggling for a long time, Trixie decided to stand up.\n\nTirek’s memory of ponies had never been very clear, and Trixie’s bad reputation as a reckless free magician also obscured her connections with the M6 and Starlight; Cozy Glow just wanted a pony, and the war-weary Trixie performing penance in front of her was still an option; only Chrysalis still remembered, the team that took the Chrysalis Hive from her hoof back then. In the end, with the promotion of Tirek and Cozy Glow, despite Chrysalis’ strong opposition, Trixie was appointed the temporary head of security in Ponyville, and thus Trixie began her controversial “detour to salvation”.\n\nFrom the temporary head of security in Ponyville, to the temporary mayor, to the official mayor, the temporary district head, the official district head, the regional governor, Trixie walked between the oppression of Cozy Glow and the resistance of the residents of Ponyville, carefully seeking a balance. Perhaps some ponies would say that Trixie’s promotion came from one accident after another - especially the “Ghost Train” accident, but is luck also part of her strength? In any case, finally, when the Empire was in trouble and rebellion was rampant, the Equestria Empire was reorganized into a feudal system. The area around Ponyville under Trixie’s rule had never experienced a large-scale uprising, so Trixie was considered as a model to be promoted. Although the suspicious Cozy Glow soon regretted this decision, with the surging public opinion in Ponyville, Cozy Glow could only watch as Trixie’s position in Ponyville became more and more stable.\n\nAccording to the final Equestria Empire feudal plan, the area around Ponyville will elect a leader and accept the enfeoffment of Empress Cozy Glow as the Duchess to rule these areas.\nAmong the many candidates, Trixie Lulamoon promised to ensure that the area around Ponyville would maintain economic development, normal life, and stay away from war, and this propaganda was recognized by the majority of the residents of Ponyville. Nevertheless, after analyzing the reasons for Trixie’s victory in this election, experts believe that it was because of Trixie’s special relationship with the rebel leader Starlight Glimmer, and there were quite a few old-harmonism supporters among the voters in Ponyville, so they would vote for the pony who had been closest to the M6 - except for Starlight Glimmer, who had openly resisted the Empire, the relatively mild Trixie became their choice. Some experts even believe that there is a possibility that members of the Starlight Rebels have infiltrated the voters. The Empire government immediately used this as an excuse to veto the first round of voting results in Ponyville.\nBut in the end, the results of the next two rounds of voting still showed that Trixie had a significant advantage over other candidates, and the Empire government had to accept this election result and invited Trixie to Canterlot to accept the enfeoffment. According to a secret investigation, most of the residents of Ponyville were simply afraid of being involved in the war: the Starlight Liberation Front was trying to march on Canterlot and Ponyville, and they believed that with Trixie’s relationship with Starlight Glimmer, even if the army of the Starlight Rebels arrived in Ponyville, it would probably not lead to a battle in Ponyville.\n\nWith the opening of the coronation ceremony of Empress Cozy Glow and the enfeoffment ceremony of the Duchess of the Empire, Trixie stayed in Canterlot for six days, during which Empress Cozy Glow deliberately arranged for accompanying personnel to test Trixie many times. But to the disappointment of the Empress, Trixie’s performance was perfect - during the six days in Canterlot, she did not show any disloyalty to the Equestria Empire, nor did she give the Empress any reason to punish her. In the end, Empress Cozy Glow reluctantly enfeoffed Trixie. Upon her triumphant return, Trixie immediately announced a number of economic and military revitalization policies to adapt to the new era, and in the turbulent times, Ponyville stood out, away from all the turmoil. Trixie, who had obtained the title of Duchess, was also very tactful, never defying Empress Cozy Glow in public. And at the request of Empress Cozy Glow, Ponyville honestly handed over a large amount of food tribute to the Empire, becoming an indispensable important granary for the Empire. After that, under Trixie’s protection, the Duchy of Ponyville managed to escape most of the Empress’s tyranny, becoming one of the few areas in the central continent of Equestria that was free from famine and riots, and managed to maintain economic growth.\n\nHowever, Trixie’s situation was not optimistic. On the one hand, as a Duchess of the Empire, her obedience to the Empire made her the target of numerous resistance organizations lurking in the dark. On the other hand, even as a model Duchess, rumors inevitably reached the Empress’s ears. As the Empress gradually recalled that Trixie was once a close friend of one of the most radical rebel forces, the leader of the Starlight Liberation Front, Cozy Glow began to grow suspicious of Trixie, day by day.\n\nTrixie’s rule is like walking on eggshells, carefully maintaining a balance between the Empire and the resistance organizations. Perhaps she has a deep desire for “detour to salvation”, or perhaps she just hopes that the residents of Ponyville can have peaceful dreams in this chaotic era.

